LINES = [{'id': 'rule', 'text': "In this town, every time you're rude to somebody, you turn into the person you were rude to."}, {'id': 'leo', 'text': 'My brother Leo told Grandma she walks slow. Poof. He spent all Tuesday being ninety-two.'}, {'id': 'sorry', 'text': 'The only way back is saying sorry. Leo finally said it at bedtime. His knees still creak.'}, {'id': 'polite', 'text': 'So everyone here is super polite. Our bakery hears about two hundred pleases a day.'}, {'id': 'nedd', 'text': "Except Mr. Nedd, who snapped at a six-year-old for dropping crumbs. Poof. Now he's too young for his own oven."}, {'id': 'bruno', 'text': "Then Bruno figured something out. If you're rude to a rich guy, you become the rich guy."}, {'id': 'soup', 'text': 'He told Mr. Gold his fancy hat looked like a soup bowl. Poof. Bruno owned three banks by lunch.'}, {'id': 'twogold', 'text': 'Now there were two Mr. Golds, and the real one fainted every time he saw the other one.'}, {'id': 'mayor', 'text': 'Next he booed the mayor. Poof. Mayor Bruno. His very first law: saying sorry is now illegal.'}, {'id': 'stuck', 'text': 'No sorry means no way back. Whoever you turned into, you were stuck being them. Forever.'}, {'id': 'chaos', 'text': 'So everybody copied him. By Friday the town had thirty-one mayors, twelve rich guys, and zero bakers.'}, {'id': 'swaps', 'text': 'Then the mayors started being rude to each other, so they kept swapping. Nobody knew who anybody was.'}, {'id': 'pigeon', 'text': 'My teacher got rude with a pigeon. Poof. Nobody has seen her since. Just a lot of cooing.'}, {'id': 'brave', 'text': 'So I marched up to Mayor Bruno, knees shaking, and said the rudest thing I could think of.'}, {'id': 'socks', 'text': 'Your law smells like old socks. Poof. Now I was a mayor too. And mayors can make laws.'}, {'id': 'law', 'text': 'Law number two: saying sorry is allowed again. Also, every Friday is now pancake day.'}, {'id': 'sorrys', 'text': 'Then the whole town said sorry at once. Poof, poof, poof. Thirty-one mayors turned back into regular people.'}, {'id': 'twist', 'text': 'But Bruno refused. He yelled at the whole crowd that they were all losers. Rude to forty people at once.'}, {'id': 'forty', 'text': "So he turned into all forty of them, one per minute. First the baker. Now he's Grandma."}, {'id': 'end', 'text': "He's on sorry number thirty-eight. Then Grandma told him he walks slow. Poof. Grandma! Get in line."}]
